{"name":"Spindle","hex":"#b3c4d8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Spindle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Spindle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spindle (textiles)","blocks":[{"text":"A spindle is a straight spike, usually made from wood, used for spinning, twisting fibers such as wool, flax, hemp, and cotton into yarn. It is often weighted at either the bottom, middle, or top, commonly by a disc or spherical object called a whorl; many spindles, however, are weighted simply by thickening their shape towards the bottom, e.g. Orenburg and French spindles. The spindle may also have a hook, groove, or notch at the top to guide the yarn. Spindles come in many different sizes and weights depending on the thickness of the yarn one desires to spin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Drop_spindles.jpg/330px-Drop_spindles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spindle_(textiles)","wikidata":"Q213761"},{"title":"Spindle (tool)","blocks":[{"text":"In machine tools, a spindle is a rotating axis of the machine, which often has a shaft at its center. The shaft itself is called a spindle, but also, in shop-floor practice, the word often is used metonymically to refer to the entire rotary unit, including not only the shaft itself, but its bearings and anything attached to it. Spindles are electrically or pneumatically powered and come in various sizes. They are versatile in terms of material it can work with. Materials that spindles work with include embroidery, foam, glass, wood, etc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Special-Direct-System-chuck.png/330px-Special-Direct-System-chuck.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spindle_(tool)","wikidata":"Q2416476"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg/500px-Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg/1280px-Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg/500px-Spindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spindle with cotton yarn, without whorl, representing the \"spindle-shape\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpindle_with_cotton_yarn.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Turkish_spindle.jpg/500px-Turkish_spindle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Turkish_spindle.jpg/1280px-Turkish_spindle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Turkish_spindle.jpg/500px-Turkish_spindle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern Turkish spindle is an example of a low-whorl suspended spindle where the whorl is made up of interlocking arms. Here the cop is wound around the arms to form a ball.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurkish_spindle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Wirtel01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Wirtel01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Spinning with a suspended spindle (below) and distaff (above).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWirtel01.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Distaff_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Distaff_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Distaff_%28PSF%29.png/1280px-Distaff_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Distaff_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Distaff_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A grasped spindle being used with a distaff.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistaff_(PSF).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg/120px-1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg/250px-1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg/120px-1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1017_-_Keramikos_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Spindle-whirls%2C_10th_century_BC_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall'Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg"},{"sr